   $q$The narrator says Ines "knew the rule about overheating thin glass. She did it anyway, because she wanted the bowl to be perfect." How does this detail connect character to plot?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that Mr. Haddad pressured her to rush, so he is responsible for the crack.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows that the bubble near the base was the real reason the bowl later cracked.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"It shows that her own perfectionism, not bad luck, causes the crack that drives the story.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that she never learned the rules, so the crack exposes gaps in her training.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows that her own perfectionism, not bad luck, causes the crack that drives the story.$q$, $q$She knows the rule and breaks it out of a wish for perfection, so her trait produces the central event. The bubble only prompts the decision; the reheating, chosen against the rule, is what damages the glass.$q$, 'draft', 'bcd597d4-e261-5b65-9da7-4aad26879c5e')
