-- Passage rg11-character-setting-plot-p02
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('9a4ef88a-55cf-58b8-9a48-a0854965e798', 'rg11-character-setting-plot-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-character-setting-plot'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Night Log, Ridge Station$q$, $q$2100. Wind from the northwest at forty knots.
The last observer left her pencil in the log,
its eraser worn down to the metal, and a note:
Trust the barometer before you trust the sky.
I do not know her name. I know her handwriting.

2300. Pressure falling. Frost on the inside of the glass.
The valley towns below me switch off one by one,
like a page someone is slowly turning dark.
I write the numbers the way she wrote them,
small and slanted, so the columns line up.

0100. Pressure falling faster. The sky is still clear,
every star as sharp as a needle point.
My eyes tell me the night will hold. The barometer disagrees.
I radio the forecast office anyway: snow by dawn.
My voice sounds younger than I want it to.

0300. Snow. It came the way the needle said it would,
sideways and silent, filling the footprints to the door.
I add a line beneath my own report,
in handwriting that is starting to look like hers:
Trust the barometer. Then trust yourself for listening.

0500. Gray light on the instrument tower.
Somewhere below, a plow driver reads my warning
and starts his engine early.
I sharpen her pencil, leave it in the log,
and close the book for whoever climbs up next.$q$, 'draft')
