  ('3a9cee38-5aa8-5fe3-a239-0dbb5e3a8193', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-character-setting-plot'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The final paragraph repeats details from the opening, such as the ticking stove and the board. How does this choice develop Hattie's character?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The room is unchanged, which shows that the night's events had no real effect on Hattie.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The room is unchanged, which highlights that the change is inside Hattie: she now feels she belongs.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The repeated details show that Hattie is bored and wants to leave her job at the board.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"The repeated details show that Hattie has finally met the people she has helped in town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The room is unchanged, which highlights that the change is inside Hattie: she now feels she belongs.$q$, $q$The same stove and board frame a new feeling: "for the first time, that she lived somewhere." The setting stays the same so the reader notices that Hattie is what changed, even though she "had still not seen a single face."$q$, 'draft', '1a9e65b8-39e1-50b6-902a-f3c8c4deb422')
