-- Passage rg11-character-setting-plot-p08
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('605c577f-e39f-5a04-99e4-c02099866ff2', 'rg11-character-setting-plot-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-character-setting-plot'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Box 31$q$, $q$The letters in Box 31 had been filed backward, newest on top, so the first one Samir Bakr lifted out was the last one Ilse Varga ever wrote from her radio repair shop.

Dear Teo, it began. Today I sold the soldering iron. The shop is quiet without it.

Samir was supposed to scan the letters, label the files, and move on. Ms. Fairweather, the archivist at the county historical society, had warned him that volunteers who stopped to read never finished a box. He scanned the letter, typed the date, 1971, and reached for the next one.

Teo, the young man you sent me has a good ear. He found the hum in Mr. Calloway's set before I did. I may let him have the bench by the window.

Then 1964: Teo, they are selling televisions now in the department store across the square. People bring me fewer radios each month, but they still bring them.

By the middle of the box, Samir had stopped typing. He was reading the shop's life in reverse, watching it grow younger. The handwriting grew firmer. The prices grew smaller. The nephew, Teo, moved from a grown man with his own family to a boy who had visited for a summer and taken apart a toaster.

Ms. Fairweather found him at four o'clock with the last letter, which was really the first, open on the table.

Teo, I signed the lease today. It is a narrow room with one window and a bad radiator, and it is mine. Come in July. I will teach you how to listen to a broken thing until it tells you what is wrong.

"You stopped to read," Ms. Fairweather said.

"I did," Samir said. "Can I come back Thursday? I want to do Box 32 the right way around."

She almost reminded him about the schedule. Then she looked at his face and told him to take Box 32 however he liked.$q$, 'draft')
