   $q$Ilse Varga never appears in the scene. How does the author develop her as a character?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Through a newspaper article in Box 31 describing the history of her shop.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Through short excerpts of her letters that reveal her skill, persistence and warmth.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Through Ms. Fairweather's memories of visiting the radio shop as a young woman.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Through Samir's guesses about her, which the story never connects to her words.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Through short excerpts of her letters that reveal her skill, persistence and warmth.$q$, $q$Lines such as "People bring me fewer radios each month, but they still bring them" show her persistence in her own voice. Ms. Fairweather never says she knew Ilse, and the box holds only letters.$q$, 'draft', '605c577f-e39f-5a04-99e4-c02099866ff2')
